WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.960
The SCP Foundation is an organization that polices&nbsp;
the abnormal in all its forms. Whether it’s a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:13.760
multidimensional chaos god, a big scaly monster,&nbsp;
or a very effective coffee machine, the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:19.520
takes a pointed interest in pretty much anything&nbsp;
outside the norm. So, you’re probably wondering:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.640
What would they want with Mr. Smith, a man who&nbsp;
was about as normal and average as could be?

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:31.040
Mr. Smith was a 47-year-old, African American&nbsp;
construction worker with a wife and daughter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:35.280
He lived a modest but contented life&nbsp;
- he had a circle of close friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.880
a happy family, and was well-liked among&nbsp;
his coworkers. But Mr. Smith had no idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.920
about the anomalous nightmare barreling&nbsp;
down the tracks towards him. Mr. Smith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:51.840
wasn’t just about to have his life destroyed&nbsp;
by an anomaly - he was about to become one.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.480
It seemed like a normal day at work on the&nbsp;
construction site when he received a phone call.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.720
It was the police, informing him that his&nbsp;
wife and young daughter had been involved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:04.720
in a terrible car accident. While&nbsp;
this is anyone’s worst nightmare,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:10.800
it was only the start of the horrifying things&nbsp;
that were about to happen to poor, poor Mr. Smith.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:16.000
That night, when Mr. Smith went to sleep,&nbsp;
he fell victim to a strange phenomenon:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.680
He started to disappear. While it would be easy to&nbsp;
write off as the result of mental illness - like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:27.520
a kind of stress-induced mental breakdown -&nbsp;
Mr. Smith wasn’t the only one who noticed.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.240
Or rather, didn’t notice.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.360
His coworkers would slowly begin to forget&nbsp;
details about him - even obvious things that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.520
you could glean from simply looking&nbsp;
at a person, like clothes, height,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:45.120
or skin color. It seemed that, little&nbsp;
by little, ever since his family died,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:52.800
Mr. Smith was becoming an un-person. This led to&nbsp;
increasing levels of fear, paranoia, and distress,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.000
as people whom he’d thought of as his closest&nbsp;
friends could barely recognize him anymore.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.640
Thankfully, Mr. Smith wasn’t just going to slip&nbsp;
straight into non-existence without a fight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.200
He realized early on that his new&nbsp;
condition seemed to abide by certain rules.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.160
The effects got worse in the night when he was&nbsp;
alone, but seemed to lessen somewhat during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.640
day when he was interacting with people.&nbsp;
It seemed that he disappeared just that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:21.360
little bit more whenever he wasn’t being&nbsp;
interacted with - and perhaps he hadn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:26.320
developed this condition upon the death of his&nbsp;
wife and child. Maybe he’d had it for a while,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.720
but it was the constant presence of his&nbsp;
family that kept the effects from worsening.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:36.720
But now that he’d properly identified the problem,&nbsp;
Mr. Smith could begin devising some solutions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.920
If nobody else was there to interact with him at&nbsp;
night, he’d keep his position in reality stable by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:48.000
interacting with himself. Mr. Smith would repeat&nbsp;
his own name to himself regularly, reaffirming his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:53.360
existence to himself. He’d often check his own&nbsp;
pulse to feel the rhythm of his heartbeat. He’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:59.440
write detailed descriptions of himself, either on&nbsp;
his own body or a surrounding surface. And in one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:05.600
particular stroke of genius, he devised a method&nbsp;
of recording his own voice talking to himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.920
and playing it back while he was&nbsp;
asleep to stave off reality decay.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.840
During the day, while at work or&nbsp;
just existing socially in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:18.240
he’d do everything he could to constantly&nbsp;
interact with people. That way, they could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:24.400
keep reaffirming his presence, and therefore,&nbsp;
continuing his existence. The symptoms of Mr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:29.840
Smith’s condition are somewhat similar to a rare&nbsp;
mental illness known as The Cotard Delusion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:34.080
in which a patient believes they&nbsp;
are dead, dying, or don’t even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:40.880
exist. Except in Mr. Smith’s unfortunate&nbsp;
case, the Delusion was becoming a reality.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:46.080
And this was a reality that Mr. Smith could&nbsp;
only hold off for so long. Little by little,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:51.440
the coping mechanisms he’d built to manage&nbsp;
his new life began to collapse. People in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:57.920
his inner circle truly began to forget him. His&nbsp;
company no longer recognized him as an employee.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:04.960
To the people who barely knew him, he was little&nbsp;
more than a ghost. A kind of palpable absence.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:10.960
This was the point when the SCP Foundation finally&nbsp;
got involved. They swooped in and apprehended Mr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:18.320
Smith, re-designating him as SCP-1467. It was&nbsp;
one of the rare occasions that the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:24.160
didn’t need to apply any Amnestic treatment to&nbsp;
bystanders, because - due to the nature of Mr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:30.480
Smith’s anomalous activity - almost everyone who&nbsp;
knew him was already in the process of forgetting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:35.440
him. When the Foundation interviewed a A man&nbsp;
that Mr. Smith referred to as a close friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:40.800
he couldn’t even recall Mr. Smith’s basic&nbsp;
physical traits with any reliability.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:45.360
Because of Mr. Smith’s condition, the&nbsp;
Foundation had real difficulty verifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:50.720
elements of his backstory. Mr. Smith told the&nbsp;
Foundation researchers everything about himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.520
about his family and his life before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.080
but field agents were stumped whenever&nbsp;
they tried to follow up on the information.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:03.200
First, there were the issues with the existence&nbsp;
and fate of his supposed wife and child.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.720
No records were ever found of&nbsp;
either of these people existing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:11.920
and there was no existing documentation&nbsp;
to prove that Mr. Smith was ever married.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.080
The Foundation also looked into the&nbsp;
deaths of Mrs. Smith and her child:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:20.720
There were no records of a car crash in&nbsp;
the area that Mr. Smith directed them to.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.960
But that’s not all. There&nbsp;
were also no death records,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:30.160
nor any graves ever found. The construction&nbsp;
company that Mr. Smith claimed to work for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:34.720
had no records of his employment. They&nbsp;
couldn’t find any of Mr. Smith’s supposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:40.800
extended family either. The only proof that&nbsp;
he had ever existed was his physical body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:47.520
locked in a Foundation humanoid containment&nbsp;
cell, and Mr. Smith’s own words. If you think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:51.680
this sounds like a living nightmare, then&nbsp;
Mr. Smith would wholeheartedly agree with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:56.240
you. The effects of his anomalous nature&nbsp;
traumatized Mr. Smith - he was diagnosed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.240 --> 00:06:02.240
by Foundation therapists as suffering from Bipolar&nbsp;
Depression, as well as chronic sleep deprivation.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:05.040
Though if you disappeared a&nbsp;
little more every time you slept,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:07.680
you’d probably lose a lot of sleep, too.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.520
The unpredictable nature of Mr. Smith’s&nbsp;
anomalous traits could have equally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:17.440
unpredictable effects on the nature of his&nbsp;
containment, so he was classified as Euclid.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:22.640
Mr. Smith is one of the few anomalies that&nbsp;
is referred to by his real name - at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:29.600
to his face. When referred to as SCP-1467,&nbsp;
Mr. Smith enters a state of rage and panic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:33.520
and this mistake has caused several&nbsp;
injuries for Foundation personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:37.920
during attempts to restrain him after&nbsp;
using his SCP number around him.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:42.640
Mr. Smith is contained in a foam-padded&nbsp;
cell to prevent self-destructive behavior,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:47.840
along with three audio recording devices,&nbsp;
though these were installed at his own request,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:53.440
in order to continue his habit of recording his&nbsp;
own voice to play back to himself while asleep.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:57.680
This served the dual purpose of not&nbsp;
only mitigating his fading from reality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:02.720
but also keeping him calm and docile during&nbsp;
containment, and these devices are kept in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:09.200
good working order in order to avoid creating&nbsp;
hostility between Mr. Smith and Foundation staff.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:12.800
While it may seem that the anomalous&nbsp;
effects of Mr. Smith purely serve to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:17.920
create a personal hell for him and him&nbsp;
alone, the Foundation wasn’t so sure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:23.360
The fact no records could be found of his wife,&nbsp;
daughter, or extended family was concerning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:29.200
It raised one frightening question: Are the&nbsp;
effects of Mr. Smith’s condition contagious?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:33.600
If so, he could be putting a&nbsp;
lot of people in grave danger.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:38.000
Foundation Scientists, headed by Senior&nbsp;
Researcher Dr. Thorn, devised a series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:43.600
of experiments to better understand Mr. Smith’s&nbsp;
mysterious condition. There were 22 Experiments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:49.760
in total, but things began to get interesting&nbsp;
at around Experiment 16. For this experiment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:54.640
Mr. Smith was forcibly restrained, and brought&nbsp;
into a research chamber with Research assistants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:59.920
Reiner and Dieter. They were told to simply&nbsp;
observe Mr. Smith without interacting with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:04.240
and record what happened in the&nbsp;
process while Dr. Thorn supervised.

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:10.480
At 10 minutes and twelve seconds, the researchers&nbsp;
were unable to recognize the subject as Mr. Smith.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:16.160
At 14 minutes and 32 seconds, they were&nbsp;
unable to recognize the clothes of Mr. Smith.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:22.080
Less than ten minutes later, they were unable&nbsp;
to identify his race. Five minutes after that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:25.440
they couldn’t identify what&nbsp;
Mr. Smith was currently doing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:29.840
Ten minutes later, they couldn’t even&nbsp;
identify how Mr. Smith was sitting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:36.160
At almost 40 minutes, the research assistants&nbsp;
weren’t able to identify anything of Mr. Smith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:40.000
save for the fact that there was some&nbsp;
kind of humanoid creature in the room.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:45.120
At this point, Research Assistant Dieter started&nbsp;
a recording, instructing Mr. Smith to describe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:50.240
himself on record. As this happened,&nbsp;
Smith returned to a describable state,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:55.040
curled up in a fetal position on the floor.&nbsp;
There was no sign of the restraints or the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.520
chair in which Smith had been placed.&nbsp;
Subsequent tests showed similar results,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:04.880
with minor variations in timing. Just by&nbsp;
being in physical contact with Mr. Smith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:09.680
the chair and restraints had&nbsp;
literally faded out of existence.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:12.960
Evidence was really pointing towards&nbsp;
Mr. Smith’s anomalous effects being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:16.640
potentially detrimental to the&nbsp;
people and objects around him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:22.400
but the experiments continued. They had to know&nbsp;
more before there was nothing left to know.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:25.760
The next series of experiments&nbsp;
were performed with D-Classes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:30.800
and led Dr. Thorn and his team of researchers&nbsp;
to a number of frightening conclusions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:34.080
Two D-Classes locked in with&nbsp;
Mr. Smith as he slipped out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:38.560
existence began experiencing extreme&nbsp;
states of terror and distress.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:44.080
Even when they could no longer see him, they could&nbsp;
still feel the presence of an entity in the room.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:49.760
When the two D-Classes tried to escape, one of&nbsp;
them was almost mistaken for Mr. Smith himself:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:55.440
He too was now starting to slip out of existence.&nbsp;
Both D-Classes were summarily terminated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.440 --> 00:10:00.320
and Dr. Thorn began to wonder whether Mr.&nbsp;
Smith’s condition was contagious or if he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:05.920
instead somehow able to “lash out” at others&nbsp;
in his vicinity in a more localized fashion.

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:09.760
Only two other experiments were ever&nbsp;
performed on Mr. Smith before further&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:14.240
experimentation into his case was&nbsp;
permanently suspended. In the first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:18.960
a non-violent D-Class was placed in Mr.&nbsp;
Smith’s cell and ordered to ignore him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:24.000
Mr. Smith didn’t take this well - he began&nbsp;
attacking the D-Class, who fought back, breaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:29.440
Mr. Smith’s nose. Ironically, this physical&nbsp;
attack was actually beneficial to Mr. Smith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:35.600
as the violence helped ground him in reality and&nbsp;
secured his existence just that little bit more.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:41.440
In the final experiment, Mr. Smith was given a&nbsp;
cell mate: A female D-Class who was allowed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:47.280
acknowledge him. The two appeared to become close,&nbsp;
and their time helped stave off Mr. Smith’s fading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:52.400
just a little bit longer. It’s unknown if she&nbsp;
contracted his fading condition or somehow was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:58.800
able to escape, but one day while Mr. Smith&nbsp;
slept, she simply disappeared. Mr. Smith fell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:05.120
into a state of almost catatonic silence. Soon&nbsp;
after, he began to speak again, only to repeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:12.400
“I don’t want to go” again and again and again.&nbsp;
Experiments concluded for good not long after.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:17.120
Because of his delicate mental state, Mr.&nbsp;
Smith is allowed a visit from a therapist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:21.440
every week, and before any future&nbsp;
experiments are performed on Mr. Smith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:25.360
Researchers are required to seek&nbsp;
permission from his active therapist.

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:28.400
Because of his effects on the&nbsp;
minds of people aware of him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:33.680
Foundation protocol is to terminate Mr. Smith&nbsp;
immediately if he ever breaches containment. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:39.440
Site Director has also appended a memo to Smith’s&nbsp;
file - instructing personnel to refer to Mr. Smith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:47.200
as SCP-1467 whenever he’s out of earshot. Doing&nbsp;
otherwise will incur severe punishments. Records&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:52.960
on Mr. Smith are backed up in six separate copies&nbsp;
and stored in different locations, in the hopes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:58.160
that this will prevent the information&nbsp;
from decaying like Mr. Smith’s existence.

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:04.160
Mr. Smith’s story is one of pain, tragedy,&nbsp;
and existential horror. There’s no shortage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:09.920
of SCPs that can cause XK-Class End&nbsp;
of the World Scenarios, but sometimes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:14.560
the terror of these anomalies pales&nbsp;
in comparison to SCPs that can bring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:20.720
one person’s world crashing down around them.&nbsp;
According to all the SCP Foundation’s studies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:27.200
it’s likely that Mr. Smith will disappear some&nbsp;
time soon, regardless of their intervention.

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:33.600
Now check out “SCP-096 - Look at a picture of the&nbsp;
Shy Guy in Space? Shy Guy Questions and Theories”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:40.640
and “SCP-5031 - Yet Another Murder Monster”&nbsp;
for more SCP Foundation mysteries explored!

